      "writtenOn": "2025-12-26T18:24:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes, kernel drivers should not be spamming the logs when they are working correctly. The kernel logs are reserved for warnings and errors. For more details please refer to go/greenlog. To get debug logs from a kernel driver, you can use the kernel dynamic debug interface -- https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JveBqSonGu7LQD7-aRbKXScA7Lrkd6_awEtA7TvKl8o/edit#heading\u003dh.7n60gvykqioe.\n\nFor these logs in particular, I\u0027ve exposed them via debugfs. PTAL at the `debugfs.c` file. Here is what that will look like:\n\n```\ntokay:/ # mount -t debugfs none /sys/kernel/debug\ntokay:/ # ls -1 /sys/kernel/debug/wonder                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \nbandwidth\nbssid\ncountry_code\nforce_stop_tx\nfreq\nmac_addr\ntx_rate_bw\ntx_rate_gi\ntx_rate_mcs\ntx_rate_preamble\n```",
      "parentUuid": "8628500c_8b9897a4",
